# {{ repo_name }}

Monorepo of {{ services | length }} communicating microservices, generated from
the platform boilerplate (`topology: monorepo`, D-005 / D-036).

## Services

| Service | Path | Package |
| --- | --- | --- |
{%- for svc in services %}
| `{{ svc.slug }}` | `services/{{ svc.name }}/` | `{{ svc.package }}` |
{%- endfor %}

Each service directory is a complete, independent project: its own
`pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, tests, `Dockerfile`, and `.copier-answers.yml`.
Build, test, and run a single service from inside its directory exactly as a
standalone service.

## Inter-service transport

{% if transport_grpc and transport_rabbitmq -%}
gRPC and RabbitMQ are both wired for service-to-service calls.
{%- elif transport_grpc -%}
gRPC is wired for service-to-service calls. Peers are discovered by service name.
{%- elif transport_rabbitmq -%}
RabbitMQ is wired for service-to-service messaging through a shared broker.
{%- else -%}
No inter-service transport selected yet.
{%- endif %}

## Run the whole stack

```bash
docker compose up --build --wait
```

Brings every service's app container up on one network. For a single service
plus its own backing datastores/broker:

```bash
cd services/{{ services[0].name }}
docker compose up --build
```

## Test

```bash
{%- for svc in services %}
( cd services/{{ svc.name }} && uv sync && uv run pytest )
{%- endfor %}
```

